{"key":"27b90583fac43d06","source_file":"Potts Sp - Sq.json","source_id":45827,"source_url":"concordance-spittle-ppl-sputum","term":"Spittle","headwords":["Spittle","Spit"],"latin":["Sputum","Exspuere"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Spittle"],"latin":["Sputum"]},{"english":["Spit"],"latin":["Exspuere"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE","SE"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"6669","subsection":"end"},"text":"The Lord making clay of His spittle. Explained. AC 9051:end. AE 239:19.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"4813","subsection":null},"text":"(Flames from spittle = cupidity for truth.)","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"239","subsection":"19"},"text":"He spat on the ground, and made clay of the spittle ()... The clay the Lord made from spittle on the ground = reformation through truths from the sense of the letter. AE 304:61.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"475","subsection":"17"},"text":"By clay from spittle () is signified sensuous truth, such as is in the Word for such.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"spittle","url":"/meta/potts/spittle/"}